    "message": "Refactor Playwright chat input helper script to use a centralized configuration object for timeouts and retry limits\n\n## Overview\r\nThe Playwright CLI chat input helper script currently relies on hardcoded magic numbers for polling intervals, visibility attempts, palette timeouts, and wait limits. This makes it rigid when adapting to different test environment latencies.\r\n\r\n## Proposed Solution\r\nIntroduce a centralized `CONFIG` object at the top of the script to manage timing parameters cleanly:\r\n- `pollIntervalMs`\r\n- `maxVisibleAttempts`\r\n- `paletteTimeoutMs`\r\n- `maxPaletteWaitAttempts`\r\n\r\n## Benefits\r\n- Eliminates hardcoded magic numbers.\r\n- Improves code maintainability and test reliability tuning.",
